## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical RN debugging for smooth UIs, corner-case performance tweaks, and simple hooks. It favors candidates who ground fixes in real-world constraints rather than theory.

## Key Concepts
- FlatList virtualization and tuning (windowSize, initialNumToRender, maxToRenderPerBatch)
- Memoization to reduce re-renders (React.memo)
- Image loading optimizations (placeholders, progressive loading, caching)
- Lightweight frame-time measurement for profiling
- getItemLayout for stable item measurement

## Code Example
```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { FlatList, Image, View } from 'react-native';

const Item = React.memo(({ post }) => (
  <View>
    <Image source={{uri: post.image}} style={{width: 100, height: 100}} />
  </View>
));

export default function Feed({ data }) {
  return (
    <FlatList
      data={data}
      renderItem={({ item }) => <Item post={item} /> }
      keyExtractor={item => item.id}
      getItemLayout={(data, index) => ({ length: 120, offset: index * 120, index })}
      windowSize={21}
      initialNumToRender={10}
      maxToRenderPerBatch={5}
    />
  );
}
```

